## Why This Is Asked
Contracts drift is a common risk when multiple frontends evolve independently. This question probes practical, beginner-friendly contract testing skills with a real tool (Pact) and CI workflow.

## Key Concepts
- Consumer-driven contracts
- Pact broker publication and verification
- Provider verification in CI
- Versioning and backward compatibility

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pact consumer test example (JS)
const { Pact } = require('@pact-foundation/pact');
const path = require('path');
describe('Search API contract', () => {
  const provider = new Pact({ consumer: 'CatalogUI', provider: 'CatalogAPI', port: 1234, log: path.resolve(process.cwd(), 'logs/pact.log'), dir: path.resolve(process.cwd(), 'pacts') });
  beforeAll(() => provider.setup());
